{"reference":"2 Samuel 16","book":"2 Samuel","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Second Samuel traces David’s story from his accession and the consolidation of his kingdom through the ark and dynasty promise, then into royal abuse, violence within his household, rebellion, and grief. This chapter belongs within that later movement of the book, as David’s own son has taken Jerusalem and David is fleeing.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_samuel_016_a41ae8b8635fb2364bb37ad5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}